<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-British Aerospace to supply Australian radars.</title>
<headline>RTRS-British Aerospace to supply Australian radars.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Defence Department said on Monday it would buy radars for its RBS 70 anti-aircraft missile launchers from a British Aerospace Plc subsidiary for A$10 million.</p>
<p>&quot;They will provide operators of the RBS 70 missile with timely warning of the approach of aircraft and an accurate indication of the aircraft's position,&quot; the department said in a statement.</p>
<p>The RBS 70 is a hand-held anti-aircraft missile used by the Australian Army.  </p>
<p>The radar system, which would help the operator but not guide the missile, would be in use by August 1998 under the contract with British Aerospace Australia Pty Ltd.</p>
<p>Night-vision devices had already been bought, giving the system a 24-hour capability.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
